{
  "base": "99d5e653",
  "scope": "Conditional finite-thickness collar prepared from a stationary flat H=1 slab. R=1,2 only. The central bore, all axial slices and the form of radial registration are imposed. Natural radial compression relaxes with depth on each side. Frozen material order per tag from the long preparation. No independently relaxed whole throat, dynamic wave feedback or free-mouth force.",
  "law": "Four spatial dimensions: W/chi=(J**(-1/2)*tr(C)-4)/2+log(J)**2/2 with normalized K=mu=1. Reference integral uses 4*pi*S**2 dS dZ. Present radius r=b(t)*exp[-a*p(t)], w=L*t, reference radius S=R+a, Z=1-t, -0.5<=a<=0.5. Positive p(t) selected by minimizing each side; material at a=0 welded to geometric wall. No crystalline continuation beyond the coupon. The half-order reference cylinder has a diffuse continuation inside the unloaded bore.",
  "preparations": "Both long and unit-depth shapes share the same relative interior radii b(t), reference domain, registry and material chi weights. The weights are pulled onto tags using y=1-a in the saved deep order and subsequently frozen. Individual shape-specific current/optical order fields need not coincide with these tags. J is positive analytically. The proposed constitutive law has uncalibrated behavior at large compression or extension.",
  "generalized_force": "Negative energy slope. Width varies by 4*t*(1-t)*dq. Axial work is per unit length. In the total shape work all distributed registration restraints count. Per run the first secant is [-.002,-.001], second [.001,.002], third [-.001,.001] in q or log L. Labeling those forces as physical bore traction alone would omit restraint reactions. The printed omitted-mode quantity is dE/depsilon for delta w=epsilon*a*t*(1-t); it vanishes on bore and ends, can move outer cuts.",
  "source_sha256": {
